  "verdict": "SOURCE_TEXT_DRIFT_WITH_BIT_IDENTICAL_OUTPUT. Three of thirteen declared sources moved; the decoded 64x384x512 label field is byte-for-byte the digest the sealed header asserts. The refusal is a code-identity refusal, not an output disagreement.",
  "what_this_does_NOT_license": "Narrowing RENDERER_SOURCE_PATHS to make the hash match, or rewriting predictor_renderer_sha256 anywhere. That digest is baked into the sealed PBR2 packet BYTES, so a real rematerialization must re-seal the packet and its custody chain (EXPECTED_PBR2_SHA256, the PBR2 materialization receipt, the n600 grammar cross-close). This receipt is the evidence that such a re-seal would be output-preserving, not a substitute for it.",
